🚨Who is accountable in Gurugram for enforcing the ban on waste burning? 🔥 

Despite repeated complaints on 16, 17, 24, 27, 29 Aug & 1 Sept, fresh videos show waste, including plastic, being openly burnt in Sadar Bazar’s congested lanes. I also contacted SHO Sadar on 1/9/26.

CPCB acknowledged our complaint and issued Complaint ID TW 21-27319, asking authorities to “take action” and update the action taken.

Yet the pattern remains:

sweep → pile → burn. 

Please don’t treat this as merely an environmental-compliance issue. It is a serious public-health and fire hazard, with smoke entering the breathing zone of shopkeepers, workers, sanitation staff and visitors.

We have provided evidence and repeatedly alerted authorities. What more is required before someone takes responsibility and stops this?

We are forwarding the latest footage/evidence to @byadavbjp ji & @JPNadda ji and seeking urgent intervention.

We need enforcement on the ground. Now. 🙏

